        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6c67c909-f293-5002-a50e-825f8a4d82a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross, Ringo Starr, Howard Jones, Roger Hodgson, Sheila E, Greg Lake, Mark Rivera\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Songs/Albums: Ride Like the Wind, Ringo Starr and Friends\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, guitarist, vocalist, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945 and died on June 29, 1979.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from its inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974, and again for its 2009 and 2013 reunions.\n- Lowell George was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Christopher Cross dedicated the song \"Ride Like the Wind\" to Lowell George on the album's inner sleeve after Lowell George died in 1979.\n- The album \"Ringo Starr and Friends\" included Ian Hunter, Howard Jones, Roger Hodgson, Sheila E, Greg Lake, and Mark Rivera among Ringo Starr's friends.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6505d39a-abdc-5060-b808-a668ddb3df9c",
        "text": "Page: Lowell George. Sentence: Lowell Thomas George (April 13, 1945 – June 29, 1979) was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer, who was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\nPage: Ian Hunter (singer). Sentence: Ian Hunter Patterson (born 3 June 1939), known as Ian Hunter, is a British singer-songwriter who is best known as the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople, from its inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974, and at the time of its 2009 and 2013 reunions.\nPage: Ride Like the Wind. Sentence: On the album's inner sleeve, Christopher Cross dedicated this song to Lowell George, formerly of the band Little Feat, who had died in 1979.\nPage: Ringo Starr and Friends. Sentence: Ringo's friends included on the album are Ian Hunter, Howard Jones, Roger Hodgson, Sheila E, Greg Lake and Mark Rivera.",
